IMPORT prelude

-- Insurance Act 1966 (Singapore) -- the life policy I own: whether it is void for want of insurable interest and how much it can
-- pay (s 146), whether I am old enough to take out insurance (s 147), what my insurer may deduct from what it pays me (s 148), and
-- my rights to surrender, to keep cover when I stop paying, and to take a paid-up policy once it has run 3 years (s 149).
--
-- SEAT: the policy owner -- the individual who takes out and owns a life policy (and, for s 147, the young person who wants to).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 9 March 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1966.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED here: s 146(3)-(4) trust policies beyond one yes/no fact; s 146(7) valuing non-cash policy moneys; s 149(2)(a)-(b)
-- the insurer's non-forfeiture system (what my cover becomes); the prescribed surrender-value and paid-up rules (s 149(1), (3),
-- (6)), which are not deposited, so amounts are not computed; s 151 (insurance on events other than lives) and s 152 (fire).
-- Licensing, supervision, control of insurers, intermediaries, winding up, offences and administration are the Act's machinery
-- and the regulated person's concern, not the policy owner's, and are out.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Insurance Act 1966 -- my life policy`

-- "life policy": First Schedule para 13 -- broadly, a policy insuring the payment of money on death or on a contingency
-- dependent on the continuance of human life. Asked as a fact: every rule here assumes the policy IS a life policy.

DECLARE `Whose life` IS ONE OF
    `my own life`                                       -- s 146(1)(b)(i)
    `my spouse at the time I insured`                   -- s 146(1)(b)(ii)
    `my child or ward under 18 at the time I insured`   -- s 146(1)(b)(iii)
    `someone I wholly or partly depended on then`       -- s 146(1)(b)(iv)
    `someone else`                                      -- none of (b)

DECLARE `My life policy` HAS
    `whose life is insured`                             IS A `Whose life`
    `issued by a licensed insurer`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 146(1) reaches only these
    `issued before 1 January 1967`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 146(8)
    `issued before 1 March 2009`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 146(9)
    `I had an insurable interest in that life then`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 146(1)(a); "insurable interest" is borrowed: asked
    `the amount of my insurable interest then`          IS A NUMBER    -- s 146(2)
    `it meets every condition of s 146(3) or (4)`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- a policy a trustee took on a settlor or beneficiary
    `the policy moneys`                                 IS A NUMBER    -- what the policy says it pays

§§ `146 -- insurable interest`

-- s 146(1): a life policy issued by a licensed insurer "is void unless" (a) the person effecting the insurance "has an insurable
-- interest in the life which is insured at the time the insurance is effected"; (b) the life is that of (i) that person, (ii) a
-- spouse, (iii) a child or ward under 18, or (iv) a person on whom that person is "wholly or partly dependant"; or (c) the
-- conditions in (3) or (4) are met.
-- (8): (1)(a) and (b), (2), (6) and (7) "do not affect policies issued before 1 January 1967".
-- (9): (1)(c), (3), (4) and (5) "do not affect policies issued before 1 March 2009".

DECLARE `Validity under s 146` IS ONE OF
    `valid`
    `void for want of insurable interest`
    `s 146 does not reach this policy`        -- not issued by a licensed insurer, or issued before 1967: the general law decides

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My life policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my policy names a life in s 146(1)(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `my policy`'s `whose life is insured`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My life policy`
GIVETH A `Validity under s 146`
DECIDE `Is my life policy valid` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `my policy`'s `issued by a licensed insurer`         THEN `s 146 does not reach this policy`
        IF `my policy`'s `issued before 1 January 1967`             THEN `s 146 does not reach this policy`
        IF     `my policy`'s `I had an insurable interest in that life then`
            OR `my policy names a life in s 146(1)(b)` `my policy`
            OR (    `my policy`'s `it meets every condition of s 146(3) or (4)`
                AND NOT `my policy`'s `issued before 1 March 2009`)  THEN `valid`
        OTHERWISE                                                     `void for want of insurable interest`

-- s 146(2): "Where subsection (1)(a) applies, the policy moneys payable under the life policy must not exceed the amount of the
-- insurable interest at the time the insurance is effected."
-- READING (an inference, not the only one): (1)(a) "applies" where the policy stands on insurable interest ALONE. A policy on my
-- own life, my spouse's, my young child's or a person I depend on is saved by (1)(b) whatever interest I had, so no cap is put on
-- it. Read the other way, every owner who had an insurable interest would be capped, even on their own life.

DECLARE `What my policy can pay` IS ONE OF
    `the full policy moneys`
    `no more than my insurable interest` HAS `the cap` IS A NUMBER
    `nothing: the policy is void`
    `not covered by this encoding`               -- where s 146 does not reach the policy

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My life policy`
GIVETH A `What my policy can pay`
DECIDE `What is the most my life policy can pay` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my life policy valid` `my policy`
    WHEN `s 146 does not reach this policy`      THEN `not covered by this encoding`
    WHEN `void for want of insurable interest`   THEN `nothing: the policy is void`
    OTHERWISE
        IF      `my policy names a life in s 146(1)(b)` `my policy`
            OR  (`my policy`'s `it meets every condition of s 146(3) or (4)` AND NOT `my policy`'s `issued before 1 March 2009`)
            OR  `my policy`'s `the policy moneys` AT MOST `my policy`'s `the amount of my insurable interest then`
        THEN `the full policy moneys`
        ELSE `no more than my insurable interest` (`my policy`'s `the amount of my insurable interest then`)

§§ `147 -- capacity of a young person to insure`

-- s 147(1): "a person over the age of 10 years does not, by reason only of his or her age, lack the capacity to enter into a
-- contract of insurance; but a person under the age of 16 years does not have the capacity to enter into such a contract except
-- with the written consent of his or her parent or guardian." (2): "deemed always to have had effect".
--
-- Age is asked in completed years. READING: a person with 10 completed years is "over the age of 10 years" (past the 10th
-- birthday); the birthday itself is not separated out.
-- The first limb gives capacity only to those over 10. The second takes it away from anyone under 16 without written consent. So
-- a child under 10 WITHOUT consent lacks capacity; a child under 10 WITH consent is not given capacity by s 147, and the general
-- law of capacity -- not in the deposit -- decides.

DECLARE `My capacity to insure` IS ONE OF
    `I have capacity`
    `I lack capacity`
    `s 147 does not decide it`

GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER, `my parent or guardian has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My capacity to insure`
DECIDE `Can I take out insurance at my age` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my age in completed years` AT LEAST 16                                         THEN `I have capacity`
        IF NOT `my parent or guardian has consented in writing`                           THEN `I lack capacity`
        IF `my age in completed years` AT LEAST 10                                         THEN `I have capacity`
        OTHERWISE                                                                               `s 147 does not decide it`

§§ `148 -- no deduction without my consent`

-- s 148(1): "Subject to section 150", policy moneys or surrender moneys under a life policy "must be paid without any deduction for
-- sums not due under the policy or under an agreement charging them on the policy, unless the deduction is made with the consent of
-- the person entitled to those moneys"; a policy term allowing it without consent is void.
-- (2): applies "to all Singapore policies, but does not apply to any other policy issued before 1 January 1967".
-- "Singapore policy" is defined in the First Schedule by where the policy is issued and the owner lives; asked as a fact here.

DECLARE `May my insurer deduct it` IS ONE OF
    `yes, the deduction may be made`
    `no, not without my consent`
    `s 148 does not reach this policy`

GIVEN `the sum is due under the policy or under an agreement charging it on the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consent to the deduction`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `my policy is a Singapore policy`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `my policy was issued before 1 January 1967`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `May my insurer deduct it`
DECIDE `May my insurer deduct this sum from what it pays me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my policy was issued before 1 January 1967` AND NOT `my policy is a Singapore policy`  THEN `s 148 does not reach this policy`
        IF `the sum is due under the policy or under an agreement charging it on the policy`         THEN `yes, the deduction may be made`
        IF `I consent to the deduction`                                                              THEN `yes, the deduction may be made`
        OTHERWISE                                                                                         `no, not without my consent`

§§ `149 -- surrender, non-payment of premiums and paid-up policies`

-- s 149(1): "Where a life policy has been in force for 3 years or more, the policy owner may by written notice to the insurer
-- surrender the policy" and is entitled to the surrender value (if any) under prescribed rules.
-- (2): after 3 years the policy "does not lapse and must not be forfeited by reason of the non-payment of premiums" but has effect
-- with modifications under the insurer's system.
-- (3): after 3 years the owner "may by written notice to the insurer elect to exchange the policy for a paid-up policy".
-- (4): a replacement policy is treated as in force "since the earlier policy began to be in force".
-- (5): (1) to (3) do not apply (a) "to a policy securing the grant of an annuity for a term dependent upon human life"; or (b) to a
-- policy "under which no policy moneys are necessarily payable", not being one paying on a death after a specified period.
-- (8): applies to policies whenever issued.
-- The prescribed rules (surrender value, paid-up amount, modifications under (6)) are not deposited: amounts are not computed.

DECLARE `My policy's history` HAS
    `years in force, counting any earlier policy it replaced`                   IS A NUMBER    -- s 149(4)
    `it secures an annuity for a term dependent on human life`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 149(5)(a)
    `no policy moneys are necessarily payable under it`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 149(5)(b)
    `it pays on a death after a specified period`                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- the (5)(b) saving

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy's history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 149 gives me its rights` IF
        `my policy`'s `years in force, counting any earlier policy it replaced` AT LEAST 3
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `it secures an annuity for a term dependent on human life`
    AND NOT (    `my policy`'s `no policy moneys are necessarily payable under it`
             AND NOT `my policy`'s `it pays on a death after a specified period`)

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy's history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I surrender my policy by written notice for its surrender value` IF
    `s 149 gives me its rights` `my policy`

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy's history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my policy safe from lapse or forfeiture if I stop paying premiums` IF
    `s 149 gives me its rights` `my policy`

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy's history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I exchange my policy for a paid-up policy by written notice` IF
    `s 149 gives me its rights` `my policy`
